FORMAT: 1A
HOST: http://localhost:3000

# KSeF PDF Generator API

REST API that converts KSeF XML documents (invoices and UPO receipts) into PDF visualisations.
It exposes the PDF generators of the `@akmf/ksef-fe-invoice-converter` library over HTTP.

## Supported input schemas

| Document | Schemas |
| --- | --- |
| Invoice | `FA (1)`, `FA (2)`, `FA (3)`, `FA_RR (1)` |
| PEF invoice | `urn:fdc:peppol.eu:2017:poacc:billing:01:1.0`, `urn:fdc:www.efaktura.gov.pl:ver2.0:corr_inv:ver4.0`, `urn:fdc:www.efaktura.gov.pl:ver2.0:plinv:ver1.4` |
| UPO | `UPO v4_2` / `v4-3` |

## Sending the XML document

Every conversion endpoint accepts the XML payload in two interchangeable ways:

+ `multipart/form-data` with the document in the **`file`** field. Additional metadata may be
  sent as extra text fields of the same form.
+ A raw request body with a `Content-Type` of `application/xml` or `text/xml`. Additional
  metadata must then be supplied as query parameters.

Both UTF-8 and UTF-16 (LE/BE) encoded documents are supported; the encoding is detected from the
byte order mark. Uploads larger than `MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE_BYTES` (10 MiB by default) are rejected
with `413`.

## Error format

Every failure is returned as JSON:

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "UNSUPPORTED_XML_SCHEMA",
    "message": "The XML document does not match any supported schema (FA(1), FA(2), FA(3), FA_RR(1), PEF or UPO)."
  }
}
```

| HTTP status | `code` | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 400 | `MISSING_XML` | No XML document was sent. |
| 400 | `EMPTY_XML` | The uploaded document contains no bytes. |
| 400 | `INVALID_XML` | The payload is not a well-formed XML document the generators can render. |
| 400 | `UNSUPPORTED_XML_SCHEMA` | The XML is valid but its schema version is not supported. |
| 400 | `UNEXPECTED_FILE_FIELD` | A file was uploaded in a field other than `file`. |
| 400 | `INVALID_UPLOAD` | The multipart request could not be parsed. |
| 404 | `NOT_FOUND` | Unknown endpoint. |
| 413 | `PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE` | The document exceeds the configured upload limit. |
| 415 | `UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE` | The `Content-Type` is neither multipart nor XML. |
| 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | Unexpected server failure. |

# Group Health

## Health [/health]

The health endpoint is available both at the root path and below the API prefix
(`/api/v1/health`).

### Check the service health [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Attributes
        + status: `ok` (string, required) - Always `ok` when the service is running.
        + uptime: 42 (number, required) - Process uptime in seconds.

    + Body

            {
              "status": "ok",
              "uptime": 42
            }

# Group Invoices

## Invoice PDF [/api/v1/invoices/pdf{?nrKSeF,acDate,qrCode,qr2Code,watermark,isMobile}]

+ Parameters
    + nrKSeF: `5555555555-20250808-9231003CA67B-BE` (string, optional) - KSeF number printed in the document header.
    + acDate: `23.06.2026` (string, optional) - Acceptance date printed next to the KSeF number.
    + qrCode: `https://ksef-test.mf.gov.pl/invoice/...` (string, optional) - Payload of the first QR code.
    + qr2Code: `https://ksef-test.mf.gov.pl/invoice/...` (string, optional) - Payload of the second QR code.
    + watermark: `KOPIA` (string, optional) - Text rendered as a watermark.
    + isMobile: `false` (boolean, optional) - Renders the mobile variant of the layout when `true` or `1`.

### Convert an invoice XML into PDF [POST]

Converts an `FA`, `FA_RR` or PEF invoice XML document into its PDF visualisation.
The response body is the binary PDF.

When the document is uploaded as `multipart/form-data`, the generated file is named after the
uploaded file (with a `.pdf` extension); otherwise it is named `invoice.pdf`.

+ Request Multipart upload (multipart/form-data; boundary=---BOUNDARY)

    + Body

            -----BOUNDARY
            Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="faktura.xml"
            Content-Type: application/xml

            <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
            <Faktura xmlns="http://crd.gov.pl/wzor/2025/06/25/13775/">...</Faktura>
            -----BOUNDARY
            Content-Disposition: form-data; name="nrKSeF"

            5555555555-20250808-9231003CA67B-BE
            -----BOUNDARY--

+ Request Raw XML body (application/xml)

    + Body

            <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
            <Faktura xmlns="http://crd.gov.pl/wzor/2025/06/25/13775/">...</Faktura>

+ Response 200 (application/pdf)

    + Headers

            Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="faktura.pdf"

    + Body

            %PDF-1.3 ... binary content ...

+ Response 400 (application/json)

    + Body

            {
              "error": {
                "code": "UNSUPPORTED_XML_SCHEMA",
                "message": "The XML document does not match any supported schema (FA(1), FA(2), FA(3), FA_RR(1), PEF or UPO)."
              }
            }

+ Response 413 (application/json)

    + Body

            {
              "error": {
                "code": "PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE",
                "message": "The uploaded XML document is too large."
              }
            }

+ Response 415 (application/json)

    + Body

            {
              "error": {
                "code": "UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE",
                "message": "Unsupported Content-Type. Send the XML document as multipart/form-data (field \"file\") or as a raw application/xml body."
              }
            }

# Group UPO

## UPO PDF [/api/v1/upo/pdf]

### Convert an UPO XML into PDF [POST]

Converts an official KSeF confirmation of receipt (UPO) into its PDF visualisation.
The endpoint accepts the same request shapes as the invoice endpoint but ignores the invoice
metadata parameters. The generated file is named after the uploaded file, or `upo.pdf` when a
raw XML body is posted.

+ Request Multipart upload (multipart/form-data; boundary=---BOUNDARY)

    + Body

            -----BOUNDARY
            Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="upo.xml"
            Content-Type: application/xml

            <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
            <Potwierdzenie xmlns="http://upo.schematy.mf.gov.pl/KSeF/v4-3">...</Potwierdzenie>
            -----BOUNDARY--

+ Request Raw XML body (application/xml)

    + Body

            <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
            <Potwierdzenie xmlns="http://upo.schematy.mf.gov.pl/KSeF/v4-3">...</Potwierdzenie>

+ Response 200 (application/pdf)

    + Headers

            Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="upo.pdf"

    + Body

            %PDF-1.3 ... binary content ...

+ Response 400 (application/json)

    + Body

            {
              "error": {
                "code": "INVALID_XML",
                "message": "The uploaded file is not a valid XML document."
              }
            }
